            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous coronary artery dissection involving the left main stem: assessment by intravascular ultrasound.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e39</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report describes the devastating consequences of spontaneous coronary dissection in a 36 year old female patient who otherwise had a normal coronary arteriogram. Intravascular ultrasound showed coronary artery dissection and intramural haematoma at the left main stem coronary artery. Acute coronary syndrome developed and subsequently surgical revascularisation was performed successfully.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
